    "extraction_notes": [
      "PDF SHA-256 verified as 4aa62e1c1c457343cfaee8deb9d2c98b2b44dd20d6241b16eeb060bb17c2e909.",
      "Identity verified: the supplied Nexperia BC847xW series PDF lists BC847BW as an NPN transistor selection in the SOT323 (SC-70) package; the exact ordering code is BC847BW,115.",
      "The PDF is Rev. 13 dated 1 July 2022 and has 12 pages; all pages were examined.",
      "Real curve extraction was performed from the exact BC847BW typical-characteristics plots on p. 6, Figures 6 through 9. The emitted curves are sparse approximate manual digitizations of the visible Tamb = 25 degC traces at labeled grid positions; no points were interpolated between plotted observations.",
      "The hFE table provides a typical value of 280 for BC847BW at VCE = 5 V and IC = 10 uA, and a guaranteed range of 200 minimum, 290 typical, and 450 maximum at VCE = 5 V and IC = 2 mA. These semantics are preserved separately from the digitized typical hFE curve.",
      "Saturation rows preserve the published typical and maximum semantics as separate records. VCEsat is typical 90 mV and maximum 200 mV at IC = 10 mA, IB = 0.5 mA; VCEsat is typical 200 mV and maximum 400 mV at IC = 100 mA, IB = 5 mA. VBEsat is typical 700 mV and 900 mV at those respective pairs. The 100 mA VCEsat row is pulsed with tp <= 300 microseconds and delta <= 0.02 per footnote [1].",
      "Cc is represented by its published maximum value of 1.5 pF as Cobo. Ce is represented by its published typical value of 11 pF as Cibo. Both are converted to F and retain the stated bias, frequency, and temperature conditions.",
      "VCEO is 45 V maximum with open base from p. 2 Table 2. The separate V(BR)CES characteristic is 45 V minimum at IC = 2 mA and VBE = 0 A; maximum-rating and breakdown-voltage semantics are not conflated."
    ],
    "omission_reason": null
